1
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:05,100
Prepare is where you decide
where every record goes.

2
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:06,820
Nothing moves while you review.

3
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:11,100
In Prepare, create your migration
plan, then review the mappings.

4
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:14,520
Harbor Light has 12 mappings,
sorted riskiest first.

5
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:19,160
Two need review. Four low-risk items
are decided one by one, and six

6
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,340
low-risk items are ready. Select 1200.

7
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:24,460
Misc Clearing. On the left is
the account in your old books.

8
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:26,980
On the right is its proposed
home in your new books.

9
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:30,900
Other current asset, with fixed
asset as another compatible target.

10
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:34,700
Read the rule check. It says this
mapping needs your approval because the

11
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:35,800
account name is ambiguous.

12
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:37,660
Open evidence and policy.

13
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:42,180
It adds that the 76% match is below
the 90% threshold for automatic

14
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:45,620
acceptance and lists the exact
references the rules used.

15
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:49,040
A confidence score is not a guarantee
and it can't clear a policy blocker.

16
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:53,220
Then decide, approve it as other current
asset, change the mapping or reject

17
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,780
it. Your decision is recorded
with your name and the time.

18
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:59,260
Clearing accounts deserve a closer look,
and the next two videos show how to

19
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:00,780
get a second opinion before you choose.

20
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:04,580
Routine items are quicker. The six
low-risk items can be approved together,

21
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:08,460
but only after you review the full
list, remove any you doubt, and tick a

22
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:10,080
consent box that starts unticked.

23
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:14,160
Each one is still recorded as its own
decision, and tax and chart of accounts

24
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:17,700
mappings never qualify. Some
states stop progress on purpose.

25
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:19,980
A blocked mapping has no approve button.

26
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:21,660
It shows the fix it needs.

27
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:25,700
A rejected mapping keeps plan approval
unavailable until it's reconsidered.

28
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:29,680
When all 12 are decided, approve
the plan and move unlocks.
